<title>SINGAPORE: Tong Meng 96 net profit soars 808 pct.</title>
<headline>Tong Meng 96 net profit soars 808 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     12.24 vs  1.35</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     20.00 vs 14.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   153.00 vs 17.00</p>
<p>    Turnover				  4.87 vs  5.07</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.13 vs  0.04</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.03 vs  0.02</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		0.08 vs  0.10</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		    11.69 vs  1.01</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 12.56 vs  1.66</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.31 vs  0.31</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    May 23, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  May 12, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Tong Meng Industries Ltd is a manufacturing and investments holding company. It said net profits were higher due to higher gain on disposal of quoted investments.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
